# C-lord — Cursor Rules

A short version of `CLAUDE.md` for Cursor. When the two disagree, `CLAUDE.md` wins — read it before a
non-trivial change (it also holds the Definition of Done and the staging-verification rules).

## What this is

- A framework that lets people use Claude Code from Discord. An OSS library, not one person's bot:
  no tokens, channel IDs or server-specific logic in this repo.
- Zero-config for consumers: a new feature must arrive by upgrading the package. New constructor
  parameters get a backward-compatible default (`= None`); new Cogs are registered in
  `c_lord/setup.py::setup_bridge()`.
- Python 3.10+, discord.py v2, features as Cogs, SQLite behind repository classes (aiosqlite).

## How it works (so you do not rebuild what was removed)

- One Discord thread = one Claude Code session = one tmux window. `claude` stays resident in the pane;
  c-lord types the prompt in (`c_lord/tmux.py`, `c_lord/claude/tmux_runner.py`).
- Claude's answer reaches Discord by tailing Claude Code's own jsonl transcript
  (`c_lord/transcript/`, `TranscriptMirrorCog`). That is the only delivery path. Do not scrape the
  pane for answer text and do not make Claude post its own reply.
- The runner yields SYSTEM and RESULT events only. Tool activity is read from the jsonl.
- The REST API (`c_lord/ext/api_server.py`) is the control plane, not a delivery path.
- Resolve tmux per thread: `resolve_tmux_manager(channel_id, thread_id=...)`. Leaving `thread_id`
  out silently picks the parent channel's session.

## Code rules

- `from __future__ import annotations` in every file; type hints on every function signature.
- ruff for lint and format, line length 100; imports sorted by ruff, type-only imports under
  `TYPE_CHECKING`.
- Log with `logging.getLogger(__name__)`, never `print()`. Prefix with `log_ctx()` whenever a
  thread / session / task / channel is in scope. A message that was deliberately dropped is still
  logged at INFO.
- Wrap Discord calls that may fail harmlessly (reactions, edits) in
  `contextlib.suppress(discord.HTTPException)`. Never swallow business-logic errors — log them.
- A CLI failure becomes a `StreamEvent` with `error` set, not an exception.
- Cogs that run Claude go through `c_lord/cogs/_run_helper.py`; do not copy that logic into a Cog.

## Security (not negotiable)

- No `shell=True`, ever. Spawn with `create_subprocess_exec` and an argument list.
- Put `--` before the prompt (and before any user-supplied positional argument).
- Validate before use: session IDs `^[a-f0-9\-]+$` before `--resume`, skill names `^[\w-]+$`.
- Secrets stay out of tmux panes: add any new secret env var to `SENSITIVE_ENV_KEYS` in
  `c_lord/tmux.py`.
- `dangerously_skip_permissions` is never the default.
- Every command and button asks the shared `Authorizer`; never a private copy of the rule.
- Changing `tmux_runner.py`, `_run_helper.py` or any Cog requires the security audit
  (`.claude/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md`) before committing.

## Tests — TDD is enforced

Write the failing test first (RED), make it pass with the least code (GREEN), then tidy up
(REFACTOR). pytest with pytest-asyncio in auto mode; tests live in `tests/`. No implementation
without a test. Green CI is not "done": behaviour changes are also verified on staging (`CLAUDE.md`).

## Where things are

- `c_lord/cogs/` — Discord Cogs; `_run_helper.py` drives one Claude turn
- `c_lord/claude/` — tmux pane runner, config, value types
- `c_lord/transcript/` — jsonl transcript mirror (answer delivery)
- `c_lord/session_dir.py` — Git clone based session directory management
- `c_lord/tmux.py` — Tmux session management wrapper
- `c_lord/database/` — SQLite repositories
- `c_lord/discord_ui/` — status reactions, reply splitting, embeds, buttons
- `c_lord/ext/api_server.py` — REST API control plane
- `tests/` — pytest suite

## Commands

```bash
uv run pytest tests/ -v --cov=c_lord
uv run ruff check c_lord/
uv run ruff format c_lord/
uv run pyright c_lord/
```

## Git

Branch from `main` (`feature/…`, `fix/…`, `docs/…`); never push to `main` directly. Commits are
`<type>: <description>` (feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, security). Squash merge.
